Summary
src/merchant-integration/ has a real controller and service implementing the merchant-facing payment-acceptance integration, but there is no corresponding file under test/e2e/ (the repo's existing E2E suite covers only app, auth, auth-refresh, admin, escrow, kyc, ledger, transactions, and stellar-concurrency — confirmed by listing test/ and test/e2e/). Unit tests, where they exist for this module, mock the database and guards; nothing currently exercises the real HTTP request → guard → controller → service → database round trip for this domain.

Why This Matters
E2E tests are what catch wiring bugs that unit tests structurally cannot: a missing guard, a module that isn't actually imported into AppModule, a DTO validation pipe that isn't applied, or a route that returns the wrong status code — all things that only surface when a real HTTP request goes through the whole stack.

